It's been more than three years since I last played Endless Space. Seeing that it's on sale this weekend makes me remember how much I really wanted to like this game. You hear people say that a lot about games...no♥♥♥♥♥♥ eh? Bought it, of course you want to like it.
Skip the blah and straight to the TLDR summary;
Endless Space is boring and disappointing. Though somewhat challenging, it's dull and doesn't do enough to hold my interest. End result...to live up to the challenge, I'd be doing so only for the achievements or just out of complete hardheadedness. There are plenty of better games to play, and most of us have friends and/or family that deserve more of our time than this.

If you are planning to buy this game, consider that:
• The game crashes a lot;
• You can't mute your own mic or other people's mic;
• I can't even play it at 2560x1440 because the game runs in slow motion at 60fps (it's not my GPU's fault);
• There's no windowed mode without borders;
• You spend a♥♥♥♥♥♥ton of time setting the keyboard controls if you do not own a controller;
• Tons of connectivity problems;
• In order to play on NA/SA I had to set my region to USA, because for some stupid reason the game thinks Brazil is located in Europe;
• The game minimizes everytime I receive a desktop notification and it takes a couple seconds to go back, which is really annoying;
• Whenever you accept an invite to play, the game goes back to the main menu.
I'm glad I bought it on Summer Sale so I didn't spend much money.

