Pros:
- Immersive Battlemech Combat;
- Galaxy Map and Faction War with real dropships and planet capture/control;
- Player Owned Mechwarrior Units both mercenary and loyalist;
- Solo Carreer possible as freelancer, contracted mercenary and loyalist;
- Good hearted community;
Cons:
- Takes forever to make money in-game and thus acquiring mechs/gear is a terrible grind (you'll have loads of fun right away if you have a few hundred $US to spend on it);
- Quick match has long wait queues, tonnage enforcement and map/mode votation mechanics;
- Faction matches are almost exclusively tactically focused - only very well organized units have access to strategic gameplay;
- In Facion play, you are limited to either Inner Sphere or Clan Mechs, according to which side you are fighting for;
- Mech movement animations/realism is worse than Mechwarrior 3/4 and MWLL;
- Timeline is based off the start of clan invasions but technology is not consistent with that period and many important mechs are missing;
- Weapons and heat don't obey normal Battletech rules;
- Mech customization is very limited;
- Mechlab sucks;
- Out-of-match GUI (menus) sucks;
- Mechlab sucks in every possible way;
- Almost no maps require thermal vision to be used now, rendering it a near-useless mechanic;
- Did I mention the ♥♥♥♥♥♥ Mechlab?
It will also be a pain in the♥♥♥♥♥if you're a purist, cos all of the gear, mech weapons and mech mechanics are 'tweaked' by the developers to stablish a meta that'll sell better.
I play it and have loads of fun with friends from both real life and in-game, but so far have only three Cauldron Borns in my MechBays because when I started the game some people tricked me into playing Inner Sphere and I wasted all my begginer cred on useless Catapults, Locusts, Trebuchets.
So, I do recommend this game but ONLY if you're ABSOLUTELY IN LOVE with Battlemech Combat. Otherwise, it'll be too much pain to bear and you're better off playing the MWLL mod for Crisis Warhead or any of the old games or EVEN Mech Commander 2.
